From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:23:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] runtime: enforce budgets before protected-memory writes

Allow an embedder to reject writes to protected linear-memory pages without
unwinding through native host frames. Add Store-bound signal rejection,
writable-range preflight for host APIs and bulk-memory operations, and
pre-exposure checks for unshared linear-memory growth. Preserve ordinary
resource and type limits, including both synchronous and asynchronous
limiters, and distinguish internal GC heap growth through a compatible
default callback.

Make bulk copy/fill libcalls return trapping results and handle them in
both native compilers. Version engine metadata and compilation identities
so artifacts using the former calling convention are rejected even when
optional version-string checking is disabled. Keep polling artifacts
separate from ordinary epoch-check artifacts.

Cover protected writes, cross-memory operations, denied growth, pooling,
GC allocation accounting, cancellation and existing metering behavior.
The maintained memory-write, limiter and metering cases pass on Linux
x86-64, including Cranelift and Winch protected-write execution.
